@@ -0,0 +1,260 @@
+# Qwen3.8-Flash-Next monokernel with rocKE stages and schedule levers (TP1, MI355X)
+
+This recipe reproduces, from scratch on any MI355X (gfx950), the improvements we made to the
+Qwen3.8-Flash-Next monokernel decode ([Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-monokernel.md](Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-monokernel.md)).
+Three changes, each behind an ATOM knob that is off by default:
+- **Schedule levers** on the mono's own FlyDSL layer kernels: NUMA dual-copy mailboxes (every mailbox
+  written twice, each consumer polls the copy homed on its own IOD) and per-stage entry holds.
+- **rocKE stage functions**, generated by rocKE and linked into the FlyDSL layer kernel in place of the
+  mono's stage bodies, with the same inputs, outputs, mailboxes and task assignment: the MoE (M3 + M4 + M5
+  fused into one expert-major stage) and the gated delta rule (B3, with a prologue that runs inside B1).
+- **The `lm_head`** on rocKE's MXFP4 decode GEMV with a fused argmax.
+
+Every applied change is bitwise-equal to the mono at layer level, and with its knob off the layer kernels'
+ISA is byte-identical to the mono's. Together, at MTP K=3, they bring a verify round to about 0.86 of the
+mono's time, or about 1.17x the per-request tokens/s. What each change does, and what we tried and dropped,
+is in [Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-rocKE-improvements.md](Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-rocKE-improvements.md) (ratios
+only).
+
+## What to check out
+
+| Piece | Where | Version |
+|---|---|---|
+| ATOM | `github.com/proaditya/ATOM`, branch `qwen38-megakernels` | `352229d6` plus the files listed in [ATOM files of this work](#atom-files-of-this-work), committed on top |
+| rocKE | `github.com/ROCm/rocm-libraries`, branch `users/vanantha/rocke-monokernels`, directory `dnn-providers/hip-kernel-provider/rocke` | `89209ac76656aede13abd8bb4e5e6ec371ed6a1f` |
+| Container | `rocm/pytorch@sha256:bbdaba66…` (ROCm 10.0, PyTorch 2.13.0), as in `scripts/qwen38_flash_mono/repro.sh` | pinned digest |
+| aiter | built by `repro.sh setup` | `c53e9b3f` |
+| FlyDSL | from `scripts/qwen38_flash_mono/repro-constraints.txt` | `0.3.4.1` |
+| Checkpoint | `Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-MXFP4` (`repro.sh convert`) | `scripts/qwen38_flash_mxfp4/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-MXFP4.sha256` |
+
+aiter and FlyDSL are unchanged. The rocKE side needs no build: ATOM imports the rocKE Python library from
+`PYTHONPATH`, and rocKE compiles through its Python backend and the container's comgr.
+
+```bash
+git clone --branch qwen38-megakernels https://github.com/proaditya/ATOM.git
+# only rocKE's directory of rocm-libraries is needed
+git clone --filter=blob:none --sparse --branch users/vanantha/rocke-monokernels \
+  https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-libraries.git
+git -C rocm-libraries sparse-checkout set dnn-providers/hip-kernel-provider/rocke
+git -C rocm-libraries checkout 89209ac76656aede13abd8bb4e5e6ec371ed6a1f
+```
+
+## The knobs
+
+All are read when a layer kernel or the head is built, and all are part of the build's cache key. Unset,
+nothing of this work is imported or traced.
+
+| Variable | Value used here | Effect |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ATOM_Q38_SCHED` | `best` | Schedule levers. `best` is `kernels/sched.py`'s `BEST`: `numa=1` (NUMA dual-copy mailboxes) on every narrow build (rows ≤ 4, grouped `r4g2` included), plus entry holds per kind and variant (for example `delta.r1:hold.b1=32,hold.m4=64,hold.m3=32`). The general form is `;`-separated groups `[kind[.variant]:]key=value,...`. At startup the runner calibrates the scratch's NUMA area and logs `[ATOM_Q38_SCHED numa] scratch calibrated: page mask …, bit-13 rule agreement 1.0000`. Each build logs one line, `[ATOM_Q38_SCHED] build <kind> <variant>: <levers> \| extern <stage:layout …>`. |
+| `ATOM_Q38_EXTERN_STAGES` | `m3=$FNS/moe/m3_{variant}.ll,m4=$FNS/moe/m4_{variant}.ll,m5=$FNS/moe/m5_{variant}.ll,b3=$FNS/b3,b3pre=$FNS/b3` | The rocKE stage functions to link, as `stage=<file template with {variant}>` or `stage=<directory>`. ATOM checks each sidecar: symbol, ABI, the MoE's m3 / m4 / m5 generation pairing, B3's body / prologue pairing and the mailbox layout. A function built for the NUMA mailboxes (`"mailboxes": "numa1"`) is only linked into builds that have the `numa` lever, and the lever stays on for builds that link only such functions. Each resolved stage logs `[ATOM_Q38_EXTERN_STAGES] <stage> <variant>: <symbol> from <file>`. |
+| `ATOM_Q38_EXTERN_MISSING` | `mono` | A build whose variant has no function keeps the FlyDSL stage and logs `[ATOM_Q38_EXTERN_STAGES] no <stage> function for build variant …`. The default, `error`, raises instead. With `mono`, the grouped and wide builds (8–16 rows, concurrency above 1) keep the FlyDSL MoE and B3. |
+| `ATOM_Q38_ROCKE_HEAD` | `1` | The mono's MXFP4 `lm_head` (target logits and the drafts' greedy argmax) on rocKE builds, compiled when the head is installed. Logs `Qwen3.8 mono rocKE lm_head on: <kernels>`. The defaults are the measured best. The `_FOLD` (`fused` / `keys`), `_SERPENTINE`, `_SPEC`, `_SPEC_LOGITS`, `_SPEC_ARGMAX` and `_PARTS` variants are the lost or neutral levers, kept as off knobs. |
+| `ATOM_Q38_STAMPS` | unset | Measurement only: per-CTA stage stamps on the device clock (`kernels/stamps.py`). A stamped build is its own binary. Stamps bias timings, so time with them off. |
+
+Measurement-only knobs, all off by default: `ATOM_Q38_BLAME`, `ATOM_Q38_SPIN` and `ATOM_Q38_DELAY`
+(`kernels/sched.py`); `ATOM_Q38_DUMP`, `ATOM_Q38_TRACE`, `ATOM_Q38_ROUND` and `ATOM_Q38_ROCTX_TRIGGER`
+(`q38_hook.py`); and `ATOM_Q38_STACK` (`kernels/stack.py`, the two-layer stacked launch, a loss). The
+levers that lost (`pause`, `pipe`, `prio`, `place`, `b3pf`, `dyn`) stay in `ATOM_Q38_SCHED` as values
+nobody sets.
+
+The stage functions come from two rocKE generators, run by the kit's `gen` step:
+
+```bash
+cd rocm-libraries/dnn-providers/hip-kernel-provider/rocke/library
+export PYTHONPATH=$PWD/../platform/python:$PWD ROCKE_BACKEND=python ROCKE_LLVM_FLAVOR=llvm23
+python -m kernels.gfx950.qwen38_mono.stage_moe_fused --out $FNS/moe --knobs best    # r1..r4, r2s..r4s
+python -m kernels.gfx950.qwen38_mono.stage_b3 --out $FNS/b3 --knobs tuned_numa      # + grouped r4g2
+```
+
+Both write NUMA-aware bodies, so run them with `ATOM_Q38_SCHED=best`, or at least `numa=1`.
+`ROCKE_LLVM_FLAVOR=llvm23` emits LLVM text for FlyDSL's own LLVM, which links it.
+
+## Serving with the full stack
+
+`repro.sh`'s server line, plus the knobs and rocKE on `PYTHONPATH`:
+
+```bash
+export PYTHONPATH=/path/to/rocke/platform/python:/path/to/rocke/library ROCKE_BACKEND=python
+ATOM_Q38_SCHED=best ATOM_Q38_ROCKE_HEAD=1 ATOM_Q38_EXTERN_MISSING=mono \
+ATOM_Q38_EXTERN_STAGES="m3=$FNS/moe/m3_{variant}.ll,m4=$FNS/moe/m4_{variant}.ll,m5=$FNS/moe/m5_{variant}.ll,b3=$FNS/b3,b3pre=$FNS/b3" \
+ATOM_RUNNER_INLINE_SEND=1 ATOM_ENABLE_REPLAYSSM=0 \
+python -m atom.entrypoints.openai_server --model Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-MXFP4 --trust-remote-code -tp 1 \
+  --max-num-seqs 4 --max-model-len 10240 --gpu-memory-utilization 0.9 --hf-overrides '{"_multimodal_config": null}' \
+  --method mtp --num-speculative-tokens 3
+```
+
+## Reproducing
+
+One script, `scripts/qwen38_rocke/repro_rocke_mono.sh`, runs everything in `repro.sh`'s container and
+`$WORK` environment. Run it on the host, from the ATOM checkout:
+
+```bash
+export MODEL=/path/to/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-MXFP4 ROCKE_ROOT=/path/to/rocm-libraries GPU=0
+bash scripts/qwen38_rocke/repro_rocke_mono.sh all      # check gen unit gate quick
+bash scripts/qwen38_rocke/repro_rocke_mono.sh full     # optional: the composed shuffled A/B
+```
+
+- **Host mode.** The script starts the pinned image the way `repro.sh` does: `--device=/dev/kfd
+  --device=/dev/dri`, with the GPU picked by `HIP_VISIBLE_DEVICES=$GPU`. `/dev/dri` can be narrowed to
+  that GPU's render node (`/dev/dri/renderD<N>`).
+  - It mounts the ATOM checkout at `/atom`, `$WORK` (default `$HOME/q38-repro`, shared with `repro.sh`)
+    at `/work`, the checkpoint at `/model` and `ROCKE_ROOT` at `/rocke-root`.
+  - The first run builds `repro.sh`'s environment into `$WORK`, which takes a few minutes, once.
+- **Container mode.** `REPRO_IN_CONTAINER=1` runs the script directly inside a container of the same
+  image. The ATOM checkout must be at `/atom` and the environment at `/work`.
+  - `MODEL` defaults to `/model`.
+  - `ROCKE_ROOT` may also name the `rocke` directory itself.
+  - Without git metadata, the commit checks print WARN.
+
+Each run writes `$WORK/runs/<UTC time>-rocke-<command>/` (or `RUN_DIR`). It holds `summary.txt` (the
+PASS / FAIL table), `meta.txt`, and one log or JSON per check. Each check prints PASS, FAIL or WARN. The
+first FAIL stops the run unless `KEEP_GOING=1`. `repro_rocke_mono.sh help` lists every setting.
+
+| Step | What it does | Expected |
+|---|---|---|
+| `check` | Checks the GPU (gfx950) and the image (the pinned digest from the host; inside a container, a fingerprint of it). Checks that ATOM descends from `352229d6` and that the new modules, tests and changes are present. Checks the rocm-libraries commit (WARN unless it is the pinned commit or a descendant), that rocKE imports, FlyDSL `0.3.4.1`, aiter `c53e9b3f`, and the checkpoint against its sha256 list (`CHECKSUM=0` skips that). | All PASS. WARN only for a checkout without git metadata. |
+| `gen` | Generates the functions into `$FNS` (default `$WORK/fns`): 12 B3 files (8 bodies, 4 prologues) and 21 MoE files (m3 / m4 / m5 × 7 variants). Writes `manifest.sha256`. Checks every sidecar: symbol, `"mailboxes": "numa1"`, B3 body / prologue knobs, MoE pairing. Later steps re-check the manifest and the sidecars before they link anything. | PASS, 33 sidecars. |
+| `unit` | `pytest` of ATOM's `tests/test_qwen4_exp_mono_{extern_stages,extern_moe_pairing,sched,rocke_head,stamps,build_key}.py`. With the GPU and rocKE present, the rocke_head GPU case runs too. | PASS, 73 tests. |
+| `gate` | Layer-level gates against plain mono, one launch from the same snapshot and tag. Each compares the layer output, every mailbox (NUMA builds on their logical view, with both copies equal), every written state pool, and determinism. Each also has a mutant that must differ (see below). | Every gate PASS. |
+| `quick` | Plain mono against the full stack, back to back twice (mono, full, mono, full). MTP K=3, gsm8k, `QUICK_PROMPTS=32` prompts of up to 2,048 tokens each (`single_request_bench`, greedy, reasoning `xhigh`), after a short warm run. Prints tok/s per run and per arm, the ratio, the verify-round ratio, the acceptance ratio and gsm8k right. Checks every server log. | PASS. Ratios as in the table below. |
+| `full` | The composed A/B with the arms in a seeded shuffled order per pair: A (mono), M (mono again, the control), N (`SCHED=best`), NF (+ fused MoE), NFB (+ B3), ALL (+ lm_head). `KS="3 0"`, `PAIRS=6`, 96 prompts. Writes `full/ratios.json` (ratios only) and `full/abs.json`. | PASS. Ratios as in the table below. |
+
+### The gates
+
+All gates use synthetic weights in ATOM's layouts (`harness/rig.py`, the runner's binding without a
+served model).
+
+- **`sched-<kind>`.** Every narrow variant (`r1`–`r4`, `r2s`–`r4s`) of the delta, qsa and delta_ple
+  layers, built with `ATOM_Q38_SCHED=best`, against the plain build. The mutant is `mutate.c1=1`, one
+  payload bit flipped.
+- **`sched-grouped`.** The grouped verify `r4g2` of a 4-layer rig. A second plain process, `best` and
+  `numa=1` must all equal the plain dump bitwise, and the mutant must differ.
+- **`moe-<kind>_<variant>`.** The fused MoE with the serving knobs (`stage_moe_fused.BEST_KNOBS`, under
+  the `numa=1` lever) in every narrow variant of the three kinds.
+  - Extra cases: forced routing to 40 and to 10 unique experts, and a step counter that crosses 2^25
+    (an old tag bug that the `xtag_or` mutant must reproduce exactly there).
+  - The mutant is `combine_swap`.
+- **`b3-files`.** The generated B3 files, as served: `b3=$FNS/b3,b3pre=$FNS/b3` with
+  `ATOM_Q38_EXTERN_MISSING=error` under `ATOM_Q38_SCHED=best`, every variant including `r4g2`. The `numa`
+  lever must stay on.
+- **`b3-mutant-<v>`.** The tuned NUMA set in situ, plus the plain layer with the lever. The mutant is
+  `exp=hw`, a different exponential.
+- **`composed`.** N, NF and NFB built into one DeltaNet layer by ATOM's own `build_layer`, every variant.
+  Each arm must link exactly the expected functions and keep the lever.
+- **`head`.** The served rocKE head (`rocke_head.build`, default knobs) at the head's shape against the
+  mono head, rows 1–16.
+  - The logits must match bitwise, and the argmax must match plain, with a planted tie, and over three
+    calls in a row.
+  - The mutant is `korder=lane`, whose logits must differ.
+- **`isa`.** Seven layer builds (delta r1 / r4 / r4s, qsa r1 / r4s, delta_ple r1 / r4s) compiled from
+  this tree with every knob unset, and from a plain export of `352229d6`. Their instruction bodies and
+  resources must be identical.
+
+`GATE_SET=smoke` runs one variant per gate, for a first try. `GATES="head isa"` runs a subset.
+
+### Expected results
+
+Ratios are the full stack (or arm) over plain mono, run on the same GPU. Below 1 is faster for time; above 1
+is faster for tok/s.
+
+| Measure (MTP K=3, gsm8k, CONC 1) | `quick` (2 pairs, 32 prompts) | `full` (6 pairs, 96 prompts) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Verify-round time, full stack (ALL) | 0.85–0.87 | 0.851–0.861 |
+| Per-request tok/s, full stack (ALL) | 1.15–1.19 | 1.160–1.180 |
+| Acceptance length | 0.99–1.01 | 0.99–1.01 |
+| gsm8k right | within mono's run-to-run spread (a few prompts) | within mono's spread |
+
+The `full` arms, per arm, at K=3. Round is the verify-round ratio, ±0.01:
+- M (mono again, the control): 0.997–1.004;
+- N: 0.93 (tok/s 1.08);
+- NF: 0.88 (tok/s 1.14);
+- NFB: 0.87 (tok/s 1.16);
+- ALL: 0.86 (tok/s 1.17).
+
+At K=0 we measured each change on its own (6-pair A/Bs), not the composed stack:
+- `SCHED=best`: about 0.89 of mono's per-token time;
+- B3: about 0.97;
+- the fused MoE: about 0.98;
+- the head: neutral.
+
+The composed stack at K=0 has only a one-pair smoke of `full` (8 prompts): ALL at about 0.88 of mono's
+per-token time, most of it from N. Treat K=0 as something to measure, not a band to meet.
+
+`quick` fails below `QUICK_MIN_SPEEDUP` (default 1.10 tok/s ratio), on any server-log check, or when the full
+stack gets fewer than 0.8 of the mono's gsm8k right. A host that is not an otherwise idle MI355X can land
+outside the bands without anything being wrong. The gates are the numerics proof.
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+- **Served text differs between runs, for plain mono too.** Plain mono's greedy replies are not
+  run-to-run identical over long generations: 0/8, and 4–17 of 144–480 prompts, were identical between
+  two mono runs. Identical served text therefore proves nothing either way. The numerics are proven at
+  layer level (`gate`), bitwise, with mutants. gsm8k counts only need to stay within mono's own spread.
+- **Every server start recompiles.** FlyDSL does not write kernels with linked external functions to its
+  disk cache, so each process compiles the extern-linked layer kernels once at startup. Plain mono
+  kernels are cached. The kit also gives each run fresh FlyDSL / Triton / comgr caches;
+  `Q38_SHARED_CACHE=1` shares them under `/work/cache` instead.
+- **The NUMA calibration line.** A server or rig with the `numa` lever logs `[ATOM_Q38_SCHED numa] scratch
+  calibrated: page mask 0x…, bit-13 rule agreement 1.0000, remote/local round trip ~1.5`.
+  - An agreement below 1 means the 2 MiB-page home-IOD rule does not hold on that host. The lever
+    still computes the same bits, but loses its gain.
+  - `numa off for <kind> <variant>` means a build linked a function that addresses the plain mailboxes,
+    so the lever was dropped for that build. It never appears with the files of `gen`.
+- **Grouped builds (8–16 rows) fall back to FlyDSL.** Concurrency above 1 with MTP builds grouped
+  variants (`r8g4`, `r12g4`, `r16g4`), and wide builds have more than 4 rows. There are no rocKE
+  functions for them yet.
+  - With `ATOM_Q38_EXTERN_MISSING=mono` they keep the FlyDSL MoE and B3, and log `[ATOM_Q38_EXTERN_STAGES]
+    no <stage> function for build variant …`. That is expected.
+  - Wide builds also drop `numa`, `place` and `dyn` by design. `r4g2` has a B3 function but no fused MoE
+    (FlyDSL MoE).
+- **A sidecar or pairing error at server start.** For example `requires`, `pair`, `needs b3pre`, or `numa1
+  ... without the numa lever`. The files in `$FNS` do not belong together, or the server runs without
+  `ATOM_Q38_SCHED`. Rerun `gen` and serve with `ATOM_Q38_SCHED=best`.
+- **rocKE does not import.** `ROCKE_ROOT` must hold `dnn-providers/hip-kernel-provider/rocke`, or be that
+  directory. The kit puts `platform/python` and `library` on `PYTHONPATH` and sets `ROCKE_BACKEND=python`.
+- **Timing hygiene.** Use an otherwise idle GPU. Stamped builds (`ATOM_Q38_STAMPS=1`) bias stage times. Do
+  not read a single run: `full` interleaves the arms in a shuffled order against a mono-vs-mono control.
+
